//Experiment 4 — Student Marks Processing Using COBOL Tables (OCCURS).
//Objective: To store multiple marks using OCCURS, calculate the total and average, and display the result.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. TABLE-HANDLING.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

01 WS-STUDENT-TABLE.
   05 WS-MARK PIC 9(3) OCCURS 5 TIMES.

01 WS-I       PIC 9.
01 WS-TOTAL   PIC 9(4) VALUE 0.
01 WS-AVG     PIC 9(3)V99.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.

    DISPLAY "ENTER 5 STUDENT MARKS:"

    PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 5
        ACCEPT WS-MARK(WS-I)
        ADD WS-MARK(WS-I) TO WS-TOTAL
    END-PERFORM

    DISPLAY "STUDENT MARKS:"

    PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 5
        DISPLAY WS-MARK(WS-I)
    END-PERFORM

    COMPUTE WS-AVG = WS-TOTAL / 5

    DISPLAY "TOTAL MARKS: " WS-TOTAL
    DISPLAY "AVERAGE: " WS-AVG

    STOP RUN.
